docs\appendix2_crosswalk.md-103-
docs\appendix2_crosswalk.md:104:One deviation from the locked document is reported. After the primary analysis was complete, the remaining harmonizable-but-unused items (public-assistance receipt, alcohol frequency and quantity, binge drinking, weekend sleep duration) were screened by comparing the direction of their adjusted associations with depression across the three cohorts. This screening inspected NHANES outcome associations and so lies outside the locked plan; it is reported in Methods §2.5.1 as a post-hoc diagnostic. It did not change the predictor set: no item was added, because those with a consistent direction added no external discrimination (ΔAUROC <0.001) and the remainder reversed direction between countries.
