192: Other pre-specified rules and their disposition: the parsimony margin was tightened from the recommended 0.02 to 0.01 (both reported, กื3.6); the operating point was reported both at the recommended sensitivity กร0.85 and at the alternative Youden point (Tables S1 and S4); unweighted training with weighted evaluation was used as the primary approach with weighted training as sensitivity, as recommended; the planned self-reported-versus-measured BMI comparison and the prior-depression-diagnosis exclusion could not be run because KCHS records only self-reported BMI and no prior diagnosis (กื4.4); an alternative physical-activity definition was not available in the harmonized data, which carries only the binary aerobic-recommendation indicator; and the planned R components were not used ? all analyses ran in Python (กื2.12).
