docs\manuscript_17var.md:194:**Figure legends.** Figure 1: Weighted sample characteristics across cohorts?”panel A, prevalence/proportion; panel B, means (exact values in Multimedia Appendix 3, Table S6). Figure 2: Calibration plots (internal, NHANES pre, NHANES post; original probabilities). Figure 3: Receiver operating characteristic curves (weighted) for internal, NHANES pre, and NHANES post. Figure 4: Sensitivity analyses?”weighted AUROC across specifications for internal, NHANES pre, and NHANES post (exact values in Multimedia Appendix 3, Table S7). Figure 5: Global SHAP importance of the 17 predictors (KCHS). Figure 6: Subgroup discrimination (weighted AUROC with 95% CIs) by sex, age, and education (KCHS hold-out) and by race/ethnicity (NHANES pre and post). Figure 7: Decision curves (weighted net benefit) for the three datasets, each with its own screen-all and screen-none default strategies; original, non-recalibrated probabilities. Tables: Table 1 (harmonized predictor set) and Table 2 (discrimination and calibration).
docs\manuscript_17var.md:217:- **Multimedia Appendix 3.** Clinical utility, characteristics, and sensitivity analyses: reference-threshold operating characteristics (Table S1), triage-oriented high-sensitivity operating points (Table S4), decision-curve net benefit (Table S5), weighted sample characteristics (Table S6), full sensitivity-analysis table (Table S7), the parsimonious-model item-count trajectory (Table S8), subgroup discrimination and calibration with CIs (Table S9), depression-module non-response (Table S10), and the disposition of every pre-specified rule (Table S11).
